  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, adapted from recipe 3 in docs/agents/recipes.md. `typecheck` passes. I did not run `vite build` or open the scene in a browser, so the rendering and the key presses are untested.\n\n- **Scene:** `/assets/soldier.glb` is loaded with `targetHeight` 1.8 and stands on a 12×12 ground plane. The camera is a perspective camera that frames the whole character. One shadow-casting directional light and a hemisphere fill light light the scene.\n- **Animation:** The soldier starts on `Idle`. `R` cross-fades to `Run` and `I` cross-fades back to `Idle`, each over 0.4 s.\n- **`window.__EVAL__`:** `clip()` returns the target clip name as soon as a fade starts.\n- **`window.__EVAL_READY__`:** It is set to true after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nI copied the model's sha256 and animation list from the recipe instead of computing them from the file. I couldn't check them, since I have no shell. That is the likeliest cause if the model fails to load.\n\nI left `castShadow: false` on the ground plane, as in the recipe. The plane should still receive the character's shadow, but I haven't seen it rendered.\n\n",
